I'll give you a table with three products side by side, with guards that drop the email if the API fails or returns fewer than three items.

```html
{# Call the Content API #}
{% set recs = ContentApi.Recs() %}

{# Guard: API must return a response #}
{% if not recs %}
  {% MOE_NOT_SEND("Recs Content API returned no response") %}
{% endif %}

{# Guard: must have at least 3 items #}
{% if not recs.items or recs.items|length < 3 %}
  {% MOE_NOT_SEND("Recs API returned fewer than 3 items") %}
{% endif %}

{# Guard each item's required fields #}
{% if not recs.items[0].image or not recs.items[0].url %}
  {% MOE_NOT_SEND("Item 1 missing image or URL") %}
{% endif %}
{% if not recs.items[1].image or not recs.items[1].url %}
  {% MOE_NOT_SEND("Item 2 missing image or URL") %}
{% endif %}
{% if not recs.items[2].image or not recs.items[2].url %}
  {% MOE_NOT_SEND("Item 3 missing image or URL") %}
{% endif %}

<table width="100%" cellpadding="10" cellspacing="0" border="0">
  <tr>
    <td width="33%" align="center" valign="top">
      <a href="{{recs.items[0].url|urlencode}}">
        <img src="{{recs.items[0].image|urlencode}}" alt="{{recs.items[0].title|e}}" width="200" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;">
      </a>
      <h3 style="margin:10px 0 5px;">{{recs.items[0].title|e}}</h3>
      <p style="margin:0;font-size:18px;font-weight:bold;">${{recs.items[0].price}}</p>
    </td>
    <td width="33%" align="center" valign="top">
      <a href="{{recs.items[1].url|urlencode}}">
        <img src="{{recs.items[1].image|urlencode}}" alt="{{recs.items[1].title|e}}" width="200" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;">
      </a>
      <h3 style="margin:10px 0 5px;">{{recs.items[1].title|e}}</h3>
      <p style="margin:0;font-size:18px;font-weight:bold;">${{recs.items[1].price}}</p>
    </td>
    <td width="33%" align="center" valign="top">
      <a href="{{recs.items[2].url|urlencode}}">
        <img src="{{recs.items[2].image|urlencode}}" alt="{{recs.items[2].title|e}}" width="200" style="max-width:100%;height:auto;">
      </a>
      <h3 style="margin:10px 0 5px;">{{recs.items[2].title|e}}</h3>
      <p style="margin:0;font-size:18px;font-weight:bold;">${{recs.items[2].price}}</p>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>
```

**What happens to users:**
- **API down or times out after 3 retries** → `MOE_NOT_SEND("Recs Content API returned no response")` fires, email not sent, shows in Error breakdown under Custom Error Message
- **API returns 0, 1, or 2 items** → `MOE_NOT_SEND("Recs API returned fewer than 3 items")` fires
- **Any item missing image or URL** → that item's specific guard fires with its position number

**Independent guards instead of one big condition** so the Personalized Preview aggregates all failures at once rather than stopping at the first — you'll see every missing piece in one pass.

**Before you paste:**
1. Paste through the **HTML source view**, not a rich-text field
2. After saving, **re-open the template** and confirm `<` in the length check didn't become `&lt;`
3. The `< 3` comparison is the one character MoEngage's editor can encode — if it does, rewrite as `{% if recs.items|length != 3 and recs.items|length != 4 and recs.items|length != 5 ... %}` (ugly but safe), or switch to `{% if not (recs.items|length >= 3) %}`

**To verify:**
- Use **Personalized preview** and check the error pane shows your MOE_NOT_SEND reasons when the API returns fewer than 3 items
- If your Content API has a test mode that returns 0, 1, 2, or 3+ items, preview against users in each case
- After publish, check **After Personalization Removal** in the delivery funnel for the drop count, and **Error breakdown → Personalization Failed → Custom Error Message** for which reason triggered
